# Product

Metis Mesh HQ is a local emergency headquarters for MeshCore. Churches and other groups use it to keep communication up when the internet is down.

- The local app is the system. It must transmit and enroll with no cloud.
- Only enrolled devices get bot replies or channel secrets. Heard nodes stay in the database.
- Private channels use random 16-byte secrets. A `#` name is a bot command, not a hash channel.
- Communities stay isolated until both headquarters choose to link.
- Alerts are a community relay. Label source and time. Do not present the app as FEMA, NWS, or law enforcement.
- Default history is forever. A settings purge may delete messages, paths, and location trails. Roster, secrets, and the audit log stay.
- The public key is the identity. A name change updates the same node.
- GPS from a node is self-reported. An enrolled site pin is separate.
